---
description: Slurm --output log naming convention (no descriptor prefix)
globs: scripts/**/*.sbatch
alwaysApply: true
---

# Slurm `--output` naming

When writing `#SBATCH --output=` in any sbatch script, **do NOT prepend
a job descriptor** (e.g. `probe_rf_bs_`, `tune_rf_steps_`, `rf_l96_neurips_`).
The user relies on a `printlog` alias + shell autocomplete in the
`slurm_output/` directory; descriptor prefixes make those slow to type.

Use the bare Slurm patterns only: `%A_%a.log` for array jobs, `%j.log` for
single-task jobs.

- Do NOT change existing sbatch scripts that already use a descriptor
  prefix unless the user asks — they were written before this rule.
- The job name (`#SBATCH --job-name=...`) and the per-task `RUN_DIR`
  / `RUN_NAME` inside `logs/` can and should still carry descriptive
  prefixes; this rule only constrains the top-level `--output` path.

```sbatch
# BAD
#SBATCH --output=/projects/.../slurm_output/probe_rf_bs_%A_%a.log
#SBATCH --output=/projects/.../slurm_output/eval_lfppf_%j.log

# GOOD
#SBATCH --output=/projects/.../slurm_output/%A_%a.log
#SBATCH --output=/projects/.../slurm_output/%j.log
```
